The purpose of this call is to identify and support projects that can foster EU Code Week’s mission to promote coding, computational thinking, and digital skills across Europe.
 The aim is to identify projects that can achieve large-scale impact and deliver on key EU Code Week performance indicators within the project implementation period. 
 Key tasks: 
 - Supporting the organisation of a large number of impactful coding, computational thinking, digital skills, and STEM activities; 
- Increasing the number of activities registered on the EU Code Week platform; 
- Reaching a large number of participants through local, regional, national, or cross-border activities; 
- Increasing the participation of girls and young women in coding, digital skills, and STEM education; 
- Supporting career-focused events that introduce students to educational and professional opportunities in STEM and digital fields; 
- Supporting university visits and other activities that strengthen connections between schools, students, and higher-education institutions; 
- Supporting activities and approaches that can be replicated or scaled beyond the project implementation period. 
 Priority will be given to projects that can deliver a large number of activities to the EU Code Week platform and participants while maintaining educational quality and demonstrating clear and measurable impact.

